<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n277" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγα-κλεής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
		voc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κλεές</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					17.716
				</span></i>
			, al.: 
				Ep.
			 gen. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγακλῆος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.738
				</span></i>
			, nom. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγακληεῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Man.
					3.324
				</span></i>
			: shortened acc. sing. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγακλέᾰ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					9.106
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>I.</u>
				1.34
			</span></i>; dat. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγακλέϊ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>APl.</u>
					5.377
				</span></i>
			; acc. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγακλέᾰς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antim.
					<u>Eleg.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			:—<i>very glorious, famous,</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> always of men, as <i><span class="en">
				16.738
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				23.529
			</span></i>; later of places and things, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναός,
				Δᾶλος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
				15.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>Pae.</u>
				4.12
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιάν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				5.48
			</span></i>.—
				Ep.
			 and Lyr. word (not in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>), exc. in Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγακλεῶς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Praec.</u>
				12
			</span></i>.</div>
